Annual inspections to allow the continuation of business shall be completed by the code enforcement officer, or designee, at the discretion of the city administrator, and the tire establishment may be allowed to continue business, provided that:
(1) The applicant, including partners, members of the limited liability company or officers of the corporation, as applicable, have not been convicted within the previous five years of two or more violations of this article;
(2) After inspection, the premises are in compliance with this article and other applicable city ordinances and codes. In the event an establishment fails an inspection, the applicant may request re-inspection for an additional $100.00 re-inspection fee;
(3) A business shall at all times display proof of the completion of its most recent inspection issued under this section. Said proof of completion must be displayed in a manner and location approved by the building official; and
(4) If a business fails an inspection and/or re-inspection causing the cessation of business, the results of the inspection shall be appealable in accordance with section 38-12.
(Ord. of 12-1-2022)

